# What must never reach a build context, and what would only make it slower.
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS A SECURITY BOUNDARY, not tidiness. `03-deployment-model.md`
# §1.2 requires "no secret in any layer", and a build context is a layer: a
# `COPY . .` in the build stage would put anything listed here into the image
# even if the final stage never copies it forward, because intermediate layers
# are still layers.

secrets/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Build output and caches — regenerated inside the image, and copying them in
# would let a stale local build shadow the one the Dockerfile just made.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
out
coverage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
test-results
playwright-report

# Not part of the application.
#
# `tests/` is deliberately NOT excluded: `next build` runs `tsc` over the whole
# project, and `scripts/setup-test-db.ts` imports from it, so excluding it turns
# the build into a type error about a missing module. It reaches the BUILD stage
# only — the runner copies build output, never the context.
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
ai-agents
environments
npm-debug.log*
**/bin
**/obj
